<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Septennial Act 1716</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1716</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Septennial Act</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Septennial Act 1716 was a law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-great-britain">Parliament of Great Britain</a> that extended the maximum life of a parliament from three to seven years. Passed by the Whig government soon after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Jacobite rising of 1715</a>, it postponed an election the Whigs feared to lose and helped them keep power for decades. The limit remained until the Parliament Act 1911 reduced it to five years.</p></div>
